3. RESTRICTIONS & CONDITIONS

   3.1 Change Disclosure Requirement (Open Source Only)
   If You distribute a Modified Version under Section 2.1, You MUST 
   include a prominent, machine-readable notice in all source files, 
   documentation, and distribution metadata stating:
   (a) that the Software has been modified from the original NimLib;
   (b) the date(s) of modification;
   (c) a clear, itemized summary of changes (e.g., via CHANGELOG, 
       commit history, or header comments).

   Example Notice:
   "This version of NimLib was modified by [Name/Entity] on [Date].
   Changes: [Specific, verifiable description of modifications]."

   3.2 Commercial Modification Prohibition
   You may NOT create, distribute, or use a Modified Version of the 
   Software in any Commercial Application. This prohibition expressly 
   includes: reverse engineering, decompiling, disassembling, runtime 
   patching, dynamic configuration that alters core behavior, plugin 
   systems that override fundamental functionality, or any technique 
   that results in functional deviation from the unmodified Software 
   as provided by ArtikLamartik. The Software must be used in its 
   exact, unaltered form in Commercial Applications.

   3.3 Subscription & Recurring Payment Prohibition
   You may NOT charge Subscriptions, recurring fees, usage-based 
   licensing, or any monetization model tied to access, functionality, 
   or value derived from the Software. This prohibition applies to:
   (a) software products incorporating the Software;
   (b) hosted services, SaaS platforms, managed offerings, or cloud 
       deployments that rely on the Software;
   (c) support, maintenance, or enterprise agreements where the 
       underlying value proposition depends on the Software.

